<title>USA: Pulitzer stake cut by Gabelli group.</title>
<headline>Pulitzer stake cut by Gabelli group.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by New York investment manager Mario Gabelli said Friday it cut its stake in Pulitzer Publishing Co to 715,828 common shares or 11.15 percent.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said its latest transactions include selling 20,059 common shares between Dec 18, 1996, and Feb 18 at $45.7188 to $49.3750 per share.</p>
<p>Pulitzer, based in St. Louis, Mo., is in newspaper publishing and television and radio broadcasting.</p>
</text>
